# The brazier room below the dungeon, its stones, hourglass and iron knights, and the trapdoor's chute (Dungeon Expansion
# Plan C4, docs/regions/castle_ravenloft_larders.md §17). The lines were drafted by Gemini through the ai-bridge and
# edited here (docs/plans/gemini_dungeon/C4/); none of them is voiced yet. Our own invention, not the book's text.
#
# The seven stones (violet, orange, red, green, indigo, blue, yellow) carry the party, by `move`, to a place it has been to:
# the Tsolenka guard tower, the castle's roofs, Van Richten's tower, the catacombs, the Rooms of Weeping, the Amber Temple
# (once the Tsolenka gate is open) and Strahd's tomb. A stone whose place the party has not visited is only a pebble.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The brazier (prop brazier_brazier)

~ brazier
if flag.brazier_golems_beaten
Narrator: The white flame still burns without heat and the seven coloured stones still wait in their cups. There is no one left in the alcoves to mind what you touch.
else
Narrator: Seven smooth stones of different colours rest in cup-shaped hollows round the brazier rim. Between them, the tall white fire burns as cold as well water.
endif
if not (visited:tsolenka_pass_guard_tower or visited:castle_ravenloft_spires_roofs or visited:van_richtens_tower_interior or visited:castle_ravenloft_catacombs or visited:castle_ravenloft_court_weeping or (visited:amber_temple_entrance and flag.tsolenka_gate_open) or visited:castle_ravenloft_catacombs_strahd)
Narrator: The seven stones gleam in their hollows like bright pebbles from a riverbed. Without knowing the places in the verse, one colour is as blind a leap as another.
endif
-> menu

~ menu
* [if visited:tsolenka_pass_guard_tower] Throw the violet stone into the fire. -> violet
* [if visited:castle_ravenloft_spires_roofs] Throw the orange stone into the fire. -> orange
* [if visited:van_richtens_tower_interior] Throw the red stone into the fire. -> red
* [if visited:castle_ravenloft_catacombs] Throw the green stone into the fire. -> green
* [if visited:castle_ravenloft_court_weeping] Throw the indigo stone into the fire. -> indigo
* [if visited:amber_temple_entrance and flag.tsolenka_gate_open] Throw the blue stone into the fire. -> blue
* [if visited:castle_ravenloft_catacombs_strahd] Throw the yellow stone into the fire. -> yellow
* [if not flag.brazier_golems_beaten] Kick the stone brazier over. -> kick
* Read the verse cut around the hourglass. -> verse
* Leave the brazier alone. -> END

~ violet
Narrator: The violet stone drops in, the cold flame turns purple, and the first grains of sand begin to fall.
-> step_menu_violet

~ step_menu_violet
* Step into the coloured fire. -> go_violet
* Let the fire turn white again and step back. -> END

~ go_violet
Narrator: You step into the coloured flame and feel no heat at all, only a sudden rush like falling upward through cold water. Then the stone floor of the brazier room is gone.
time +5
move tsolenka_pass_guard_tower

~ orange
Narrator: You cast the orange stone in, the fire flares like autumn leaves, and the hanging sand begins to run.
-> step_menu_orange

~ step_menu_orange
* Step into the coloured fire. -> go_orange
* Let the fire turn white again and step back. -> END

~ go_orange
Narrator: You step into the coloured flame and feel no heat at all, only a sudden rush like falling upward through cold water. Then the stone floor of the brazier room is gone.
time +5
move castle_ravenloft_spires_roofs

~ red
Narrator: The red stone sinks into the brazier, turning the cold flame blood-bright as the sand starts to slip down.
-> step_menu_red

~ step_menu_red
* Step into the coloured fire. -> go_red
* Let the fire turn white again and step back. -> END

~ go_red
Narrator: You step into the coloured flame and feel no heat at all, only a sudden rush like falling upward through cold water. Then the stone floor of the brazier room is gone.
time +5
move van_richtens_tower_interior

~ green
Narrator: You toss the green stone into the fire, waking a pale sickly glow as the sand begins its fall.
-> step_menu_green

~ step_menu_green
* Step into the coloured fire. -> go_green
* Let the fire turn white again and step back. -> END

~ go_green
Narrator: You step into the coloured flame and feel no heat at all, only a sudden rush like falling upward through cold water. Then the stone floor of the brazier room is gone.
time +5
move castle_ravenloft_catacombs:from_tunnel

~ indigo
Narrator: The indigo stone vanishes into the flame, dyeing it the colour of a bruise while the sand starts to trickle.
-> step_menu_indigo

~ step_menu_indigo
* Step into the coloured fire. -> go_indigo
* Let the fire turn white again and step back. -> END

~ go_indigo
Narrator: You step into the coloured flame and feel no heat at all, only a sudden rush like falling upward through cold water. Then the stone floor of the brazier room is gone.
time +5
move castle_ravenloft_court_weeping

~ blue
Narrator: You drop the blue stone in, the tall flame turns the colour of winter ice, and the sand begins to pour.
-> step_menu_blue

~ step_menu_blue
* Step into the coloured fire. -> go_blue
* Let the fire turn white again and step back. -> END

~ go_blue
Narrator: You step into the coloured flame and feel no heat at all, only a sudden rush like falling upward through cold water. Then the stone floor of the brazier room is gone.
time +5
move amber_temple_entrance

~ yellow
Narrator: The yellow stone strikes the brazier, turning the cold fire to pale gold as the sand starts to run.
-> step_menu_yellow

~ step_menu_yellow
* Step into the coloured fire. -> go_yellow
* Let the fire turn white again and step back. -> END

~ go_yellow
Narrator: You step into the coloured flame and feel no heat at all, only a sudden rush like falling upward through cold water. Then the stone floor of the brazier room is gone.
time +5
move castle_ravenloft_catacombs_strahd

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The hourglass (prop brazier_hourglass)

~ hourglass
Narrator: The hourglass hangs in the empty air with all its pale sand gathered in the upper bulb. Around its base, a quiet hand has cut a verse into the stone.
* Read the verse cut around the hourglass. -> verse
* [if not flag.brazier_golems_beaten] Strike the hanging hourglass. -> strike_glass
* Leave the hourglass alone. -> END

~ verse
Narrator: Violet casts you high where the white watchtower freezes in the mountain pass, keeping its cold vigil above the snow.
Narrator: Orange lifts you to the wet slate and high peaks of this very house, under a sky that never clears.
Narrator: Red sends you to a tall house of old books and older scars, where a hunter of monsters keeps his watch.
Narrator: Green drops you one floor deeper into the quiet dark, where the cold stone boxes of this house are kept in rows.
Narrator: Indigo brings you to the perfumed dark of the sleeping rooms, where the master's brides lie in their long, unbreathing sleep.
Narrator: Blue carries you into the mountain's heart and its house of ancient amber, where old dark powers first learned to speak.
Narrator: Yellow lays you down in the deepest vault of all, beside the master's own cold bed of earth and stone.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The iron knights (props brazier_knight_*)

~ knight
Narrator: Two huge figures of black iron stand in deep alcoves with their visors down. They do not breathe, which saves them a great deal of trouble down here.
* Strike one of the iron knights. -> strike_knight
* Leave the iron knights alone. -> END

# The golem wakes only if the brazier, the hourglass or either knight is attacked. Only the knight in the west alcove is a
# golem; its twin is empty armour. It is the plan's boss fight (3 in 8 for the full-ability party, docs/story/boss_fights.md);
# every way into it is a choice.
~ strike_knight
set brazier_golems_awake
Narrator: Your blow rings against the black plate like a tolled bell, loud enough to wake the vault. In the western shadow, one heavy visor grates open: only one.
combat brazier_golems

~ strike_glass
set brazier_golems_awake
Narrator: The hanging glass chimes like struck bronze without taking a scratch, though the sand inside shivers. In the west alcove, an iron visor lifts and a mailed boot takes one heavy step.
combat brazier_golems

~ kick
set brazier_golems_awake
Narrator: Cold white coals spill across the flagstones without a spark or a hiss of heat. Deep in the west alcove, dry iron joints groan awake after a very long sleep.
combat brazier_golems

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The trapdoor (prop brazier_tunnel_slab's call)

# The trap sprang a step ago (trap:brazier_trapdoor_hatch:triggered); the next step plays this.
~ slide
Narrator: Polished black marble whips your feet out from under you in a long, fast slide through the dark, nothing to catch your hands. You meet the cold floor of a cell at the bottom.
time +5
move castle_ravenloft_larders_dungeon:from_chute

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The chute from the cell (prop larders_chute_mouth)

~ chute
Narrator: High up in the cell wall, the mouth of the black marble chute gleams wet and slick as river ice. No fingers made of flesh and bone will ever find a hold in it.
* [knows:spider_climb] Climb the slick chute with Spider Climb. -> up
* [knows:levitate] Float up the dark chute with Levitate. -> up
* [knows:fly] Fly up the black marble chute with Fly. -> up
* Leave the chute alone. -> END

~ up
Narrator: You rise back up the narrow black throat of polished marble, watching the wet stone slide past in reverse. The tunnel waits above, its trapdoor spent and sagging.
time +5
move castle_ravenloft_brazier_room:from_chute
